Because $O$ is the midpoint of each diagonal, triangle $\Delta OAB$ is equilateral. By a translation, $O$ has coordinates $(-k/2,-k/2)$, $A$ has coordinates $(-k/2,k/2)$, and $B$ has coordinates $(k/2,k/2)$. These points lie at $(1/2-k/2,-1/2-k/2)$ in the coordinate plane, so the distance from $O$ to $A$ and $O$ to $B$ are $1/2$ units apart. The distance from $O$ to $C$ and from $O$ to $D$ are $1/2+k/2=1$ units apart, so the region closer to $O$ than to any of the four vertices is just the interior of the square whose vertices are $(1/2-k/2,1/2-k/2)$, $(1/2,k/2)$, $(k/2,1/2)$, and $(-k/2,k/2)$. This square has area $(1/2)^2-(1/2-k/2)^2=1/4$, so the probability is $\boxed{\frac{1}{4}}$.因地制
