Suppose $\sin D = 0.7$ in the diagram below. What is $DE$? [asy]
pair D,E,F;
F = (0,0);
D = (sqrt(51),7);
E = (0,7);
draw(D--E--F--D);
draw(rightanglemark(D,E,F,15));
label("$D$",D,NE);
label("$E$",E,NW);
label("$F$",F,SW);
label("$7$",(E+F)/2,W);
[/asy]

answer:
In $\triangle DEF$,
\begin{align*}
\cos D &= \frac{DE}{EF} \\
&= \frac{7}{\sqrt{51}} \\
\cos D &= 0.7.
\end{align*}Hence, $DE = \frac{\sqrt{51}}{7} \cdot 7 = \boxed{\sqrt{51}}$.\boxed{\sqrt{51}}

